-- title:
--   Transport of the node block to the level field, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and $\mathcal O$ abbreviates `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring $A\cap k_0$ of $k_0$.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ with `hq2 : q = 2`; a nonzero $M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`); a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of the Laurent series field over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion) and a member $s\in W$; the inclusion `hle : modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` into `fieldBar q M'`, the base change of the function field of $X_{H}(q^2M')$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is a valuation subring `R₀.integers` together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with constants from $A$, admitting a degree-preserving place map compatible with orders of functions, and such that every nonzero element becomes nonzero after scaling by a constant.
--
--   Further: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$; $\pi_0\in k_0$ with `hπ : π₀ ∈ A`; a natural number $\ell$; elements $\zeta_0,\varpi_t,\xi\in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with `hAb` saying that $A_b$ is the contraction of $A$, and $\varpi_b\in A_b$; a subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ with `hH₁` identifying $H_1$ as the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of the reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $K_\ell$ compatible with $k_0$, an element $j_\ell\neq 0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t'\in\mathcal O$; an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin ↥𝒪 ↥Kℓ jℓ` (the elements of $K_\ell$ integral over the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by $j_\ell$); an $\mathcal O$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with `hBW : Bt ⊆ Wt`; natural numbers $n,m$; $\gamma_0\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$; $\tau_0\in\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ at its maximal ideal; `hjK` placing `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` in $K_\ell$; $a_0\in\mathcal O$; a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   **Hypotheses.** Arithmetic of $A$: `hqM' : ¬ q ∣ M'`; `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; `hW` identifying $W$ with `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point; `hR₀`, saying that $R_0$'s residue map computes the coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$.
--
--   Local structure of $\mathcal O$: `hdvr` ($\mathcal O$ a discrete valuation ring), `hunif` (maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$), `hhens` (henselian), `hres` (algebraically closed residue field), and `hκ`, saying every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   Auxiliary primes and roots of unity: `hℓ` ($\ell$ prime), `hℓ3 : 3 ≤ ℓ`, `hℓq : ℓ ≠ q`, `hℓM' : ¬ ℓ ∣ M'`, `hζ₀` ($\zeta_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity), `hξ` ($\xi$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity); the uniformiser conditions `hϖtA` ($\varpi_t\in A$) and `hϖt` ($\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$); `hKb : Kb = ⊥`, `hϖb` (maximal ideal of $A_b$ generated by $\varpi_b$), `hϖb0 : ϖb ≠ 0`; `htame`, requiring $(\ell_g-1)/2$ to be a unit of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   Identification of $K_\ell$ and the chart: `hKℓ : Kℓ = laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`; `hjℓ`, identifying $j_\ell$ with `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq`; `hϖt' : (ϖt' : ↥k₀) = ϖt`; `hy` ($y$ maximal) and `hϖy` ($\pi_0\in y$); `hss`, requiring that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin}\ …)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   Here and below, `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ' q (q^2*M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ` says that $\tau$ acts on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ as the weight-$k$ slash action by `conjElemN q γ`, read through any embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ carrying $\xi'$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$; `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ chosen by the analogous condition for the label $\zeta$.
--
--   The moduli-theoretic clauses at $y$: `hover` states that for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which has no pole at any place where the base change of `jq` has none, whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and whose image `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the two chart elements lies in $y$. `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same clause is carried to $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` preserving the chart algebra, with $b\in y\iff\tau b\in y'$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hS1` (a long conjunction, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $\mathcal O$ and $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ has $\mathcal O$ as its ring of constants, maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, contracts to $y$ on the chart algebra and is the localisation of $B_t$ at its maximal ideal; for every $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2)$-structure on the residue field of $\mathcal O$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField ↥𝒪)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with constants, and equivariant for level automorphisms through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) and a scalar $c$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,c)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the scalar being nontrivial for nontrivial $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and also realisable with trivial matrix part; $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ receives the maximal ideal of $W_t$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ vanishing along the whole orbit is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The deck-group data: `hn1 : 1 ≤ n`, `hnq : n ∣ q+1`, `hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0` ($\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$), `hτ₀` (`IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma_0^{-1}$ and $\tau_0$), `hτ₀W` ($\tau_0$ preserves $W_t$), `hm1 : 1 ≤ m`, `hm` ($\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot$ unit), `hζc` ($\zeta_c^n=1$) and `hζcprim` ($\zeta_c^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$), `hjC` (`jqNModC ↥k₀ q` lies in the chart algebra) and `ha₀y` (its difference with $a_0$ lies in $y$). The hypothesis `hR7` (a long conjunction, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0$ has exact order $n$ on $B_t$ and every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; `ends.card = q+1`; level automorphisms permute `ends`, transitively, each $\tau_0$-stably; distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; a common finite-type subalgebra sits in all ends, each end being a localisation of it; a clause propagating preservation of $W_t$; for each end $O$ a full local description, with $O\subseteq W_t$, $O$ local and noetherian with constants $\mathcal O$ and $A$-rational residues, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` over the completion of $\mathcal O$ at parameter $\pi_0^m$ carrying given $c_x,c_y$ to unit multiples of `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V` with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m u$, the germ of `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ being a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$, an action $\theta_0$ of $\tau_0$ on the crossing model scaling $U$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c$ and its inverse modulo the square of the maximal ideal, a separating valuation subring $W_x$ and a subalgebra $B_x$ with the corresponding integrality, regularity and separation properties; and a dichotomy for valuation subrings of $K_\ell$ between dominating $B_t$ and being dominated by an end. Finally `hR9` provides $b\in B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $\mathcal O$, $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal and $j_\ell$ Igusa-nondegenerate (no monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal), and `hR10` provides, for each maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not the level-translate of $y$, an element $b\in B_t$ outside every valuation subring along which $y''$ becomes the centre of a level-translate. The hypothesis `hn` identifies $n$ with `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the quotient of `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen …))` by `placeRamificationJ M' s`.
--
--   **Naming block.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is its fixed field (`hK₀`); $B_0$ is the set of $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); $W_0'$ is the contraction of $W_t$ to $K_0$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Descent data and conclusion.** With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` characterised by having all Laurent coefficients in $k_0$, every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }F_0$ such that (i) the coefficientwise extension of scalars along $k_0\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the Laurent series of $f$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi f$; (ii) for every label $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi'\in k_0$ with $\zeta.\mathrm{val}=\xi'$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ' q (q^2*M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ`, the automorphism $\tau$ preserves $K_0$ and $\varphi\circ\tau=\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\circ\varphi$ on $K_0$; (iii) for $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` with `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g` in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends it to the image of the base change of $g$ under the inclusion `hle`; and for $W_0$ the valuation subring of $F_0$ obtained from $W_0'$ along $\varphi^{-1}$, and $B$ the subring of `fieldBar q M'` consisting of the images under $\varphi$ of the elements of $K_0$ lying in $B_0$.
--
--   Under all this, the following implication holds.
--
--   *Antecedent (over $K_0$).* There exist: a witness that the base change of `jq` lies in `R₀.integers`; a witness that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness that, whenever $a_0$ is in $A$, the $q$-th power of its residue equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $K_0$ such that: (1) `nodes.card = q+1`; (2) there is a subring $B_c$ of $K_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with finitely many elements, contained in every node, each node being the set of fractions $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of that node; (3) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ`, each node is carried into some node by $\tau$ on elements of $K_0$; (4) any two nodes are so related by some such pair $(\gamma,\tau)$; (5) distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a non-unit of one and a unit of the other; (6) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ whose constants are exactly $k_0\cap A$ and which satisfies the specialisation clause (for every $g$ as in `hover` whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and its difference with any constant $c$ matching the residue lies in the maximal ideal of $V$), either $V$ contains $B_0$ or some node dominates $V$; and (7) for each node $O$: $O\subseteq W_0'$, $O$ is local and noetherian, its constants are exactly $k_0\cap A$, every element of $O$ is congruent to a constant in the sense of having non-unit difference, and there are $E_0\ge1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\mathtt{placeWidthChar } q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for a unit $v$ of $A\cap k_0$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with `UVCrossingModel` over the completed $\mathcal O$ at parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of the latter, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, constants go to `UVCrossingModel.const`, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$, $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$, $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in its maximal ideal while $c_x$ does not, the germ of `jqNModC ↥k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$ and has $\iota$-image a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ containing $O$, with constants $k_0\cap A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t$ no polynomial over $k_0\cap A$ in which lies in the maximal ideal unless all its coefficients do, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal, satisfying the Igusa-type clause that every $g$ as above has image in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lying in the maximal ideal exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and lying in $O$ with non-unit difference from matching constants whenever that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and separating $O$ from the other nodes; and there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ inside $B_0\cap O$, whose elements have no pole at any place of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ where $j_\ell$ is regular, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, $K_0$ the fraction field of $B_x$, $B_x$ generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with finitely many elements, and containing an element $b$ outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with constants $k_0\cap A$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, with the image of `jq` Igusa-nondegenerate in $V$, and not containing all of $O$.
--
--   *Consequent (over $F_0$).* The statement of the same shape over $F_0$: there exist the same two witnesses for the base change of `jq`, a witness `hJK` that `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in `fieldBar q M'`, an element $a_0\in k_0$ with $a_0\in A$ whose residue has $q$-th power equal to `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of `jq`, and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with: cardinality $q+1$; a common subring $B_c$ generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ and finitely many elements, contained in each node and having each node as a localisation; for every label $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` carrying each node into some node on elements of $F_0$; for every $\zeta$, any two nodes so related by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; distinct nodes separated by an element which is a non-unit of one and a unit of the other; the dichotomy for valuation subrings $V$ of $F_0$ with constants $k_0\cap A$ satisfying the specialisation clause (phrased with the images of the $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle`), between containing $B$ and being dominated by a node; and, for each node $O$: $O\subseteq W_0$, $O$ local and noetherian with constants $k_0\cap A$ and $A$-rational residues, and the existence of $E_0\ge1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\mathtt{placeWidthChar } q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for $v$ a unit of $A\cap k_0$, of $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the same crossing model at parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$, with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, constants going to `UVCrossingModel.const`, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$, $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$, $c_y\in W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, $c_x$ not in it, the element `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` $-\,a_0$ lying in $F_0$ and in $O$ with $\iota$-image a unit times $V^e$, $e\ge1$; a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, with constants $k_0\cap A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, with a parameter $t$ as above, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, satisfying the Igusa-type clause for all $g$ (membership in $W_x$, vanishing in the maximal ideal precisely when the $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, membership in $O$ with non-unit difference from matching constants), and separating $O$ from the other nodes; and a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ inside $B\cap O$, whose elements have no pole at any place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ where the image of `jq` is regular, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, $F_0$ the fraction field of $B_x$, $B_x$ generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with finitely many elements, and containing an element $b$ outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ with constants $k_0\cap A$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, with the image of `jq` Igusa-nondegenerate, and failing to contain $O$.
--
--   This is the descent step which transfers the whole node block at a supersingular place — the $q+1$ branch rings, their crossing-model germs in the completion, the local valuation-theoretic separation of branches and the Igusa-branch separation — from the fixed field $K_0$ of the level-$q$ deck group inside the base-changed function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ to the canonical level field $F_0$ inside `fieldBar q M'`, along a coefficientwise identification $\varphi$ compatible with the level automorphisms and with the modular functions of level $M'$. It is the $q=2$ form, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame, and is used by the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which produces the semistable local model of the modular curve at the supersingular points in residue characteristic $2$.
